00:22:41,540 --> 00:22:46,220
This common question is actually a critical test of a job candidate's communication

241
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:51,380
skills, so it's important not to give an unprepared response or mess it up.

242
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:56,560
Tell me about yourself is often the first question professional career coaches

243
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:59,660
prepare people for when they give interview guidance.

244
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:04,420
It's the opportunity for the candidate to take control of the narrative and tell

245
00:23:04,420 --> 00:23:07,500
their story in a way that really matters to their audience.

246
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:12,960
It takes hard work and extensive preparation to answer this question well.

247
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:18,480
When a person goes to a job interview, their interviewer has presumably read their

248
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:21,240
resume, so they don't need to repeat the information.

249
00:23:22,100 --> 00:23:26,840
But that's what most people will do, as it's their instinct to recite things that

250
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:28,160
are already on their resume.

251
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:33,200
It's important for job seekers to do their homework on two crucial aspects.

252
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:37,600
First, they are not just telling someone a fact about themselves.

253
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:41,780
They're telling a story, and stories take work to create.

254
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:46,820
Coming up with a good story means getting reflective about what made their career

255
00:23:46,820 --> 00:23:51,320
accomplishments something they're proud of, and what strengths those accomplishments

256
00:23:51,320 --> 00:23:56,840
highlight. Candidates shouldn't pick a broad general strength to elaborate on, such

257
00:23:56,840 --> 00:24:00,320
as, I'm smart, I work hard, and I get things done.

258
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:05,620
To come up with multiple career accomplishments or examples for different interview

259
00:24:05,620 --> 00:24:11,160
questions, job seekers should talk with others, especially people who know them,

260
00:24:11,160 --> 00:24:16,620
partners, friends, or co -workers who will bring up different stories than the ones

261
00:24:16,620 --> 00:24:22,000
they remember. Secondly, candidates should know what's at stake for the company with

262
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:22,960
this job opening.

263
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:28,160
What they really are asking you is, me why you are going to help me.

264
00:24:28,620 --> 00:24:32,660
If the person is a prepared candidate, they should have already figured out those

265
00:24:32,660 --> 00:24:37,500
things. They've read the job description and researched the company on the internet.

266
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:43,320
What job applicants ought to be looking for is what the company is up to, what they

267
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:47,480
are trying to accomplish, and what is preventing them from accomplishing those

268
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:50,400
things. How long should it take to answer?

269
00:24:50,960 --> 00:24:51,700
Around a minute.

270
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:55,000
That's about right for most people's attention spans.

271
00:24:55,760 --> 00:25:00,880
Under a minute could seem rushed, while over two minutes will start to feel more

272
00:25:00,880 --> 00:25:01,680
like a speech.

273
00:25:02,300 --> 00:25:07,160
But the length of the answer is not an exact science, and candidates need to keep

274
00:25:07,160 --> 00:25:11,220
their career story focused and tailored to their audience.

275
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:42,360
Question 23. What will most people do when they come to a job interview?

276
00:25:55,300 --> 00:26:02,400
Question 24. Why should job seekers talk with partners, friends, and co -workers?

277
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:23,580
Question 25. What other important preparations should job seekers make before an

278
00:26:23,580 --> 00:26:39,500
interview? That's the end of listening comprehension.
